Patch: FicTrac (neurophysiology-expertise-unit/fictrac-basler) for modern Pylon (7/8)

The fork includes a USB3-specific header that does not exist in Pylon 7/8 --
there is no pylon/usb/ directory at all. The source only uses the generic
Pylon::CInstantCamera, which drives GigE and USB3 alike, so swapping to the
transport-agnostic header is sufficient.

Symptom without this patch:
  fatal error: pylon/usb/BaslerUsbInstantCameraArray.h: No such file or directory

--- a/include/BaslerSource.h
+++ b/include/BaslerSource.h
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
-#include <pylon/usb/BaslerUsbInstantCameraArray.h>
+#include <pylon/InstantCameraArray.h>

Apply with:
  sed -i 's|#include <pylon/usb/BaslerUsbInstantCameraArray.h>|#include <pylon/InstantCameraArray.h>|' \
    ~/fictrac/include/BaslerSource.h
